  "body": "Hi, thank you for your great work!\n\nWhile exploring the codebase/documentation, I noticed that the design of \"Sample-level Rollout Lifecycle Control\" shares similarities with the RL infrastructure I previously designed and implemented (**MiMo**, released on **2025.04.30**). For your information:\n\n- **MiMo Seamless Rollout Engine** (https://github.com/XiaomiMiMo/MiMo/blob/main/MiMo-7B-Technical-Report.pdf)\n<img width=\"500\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d552e58f-76af-43f3-ae57-4174030d4cf5\" />\n\n<img width=\"700\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1e12c787-b096-4b2d-8e22-37b64b34d3d3\" />\n\n<br></br>\n\n- **ROLL Sample-level Rollout Lifecycle Control**\n<img width=\"600\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ba8a7a73-d74a-4d9d-aadd-3c54824c3fa3\" />\n\n<br></br>\n\nI noticed that some design concepts in your project—such as \"Async Reward\", \"Add Request\", and \"Abort Request\"—closely align with the approaches I proposed in MiMo (\"Async Reward\", \"Continuous Rollout\", and \"Early Termination\"). While I recognize that similar ideas can emerge independently, I’d like to kindly ask if you could consider referencing my work in your documentation (e.g., README’s \"Acknowledgements\") and technical report. This would help users trace the evolution of these ideas and ensure proper attribution.\n\nLet me know your thoughts—I’m happy to discuss further or submit a PR if needed. Thanks again for your time!\n",
